DECISION MergeRulesHaveOnePublicHome
	SPEC "The corpus is the single public source of the merge rules, one RULE DOMAIN merge per"
		+ "conflict the merge settles"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/rules.awawa"
	SPEC "The README does not restate the merge rules and carries an index naming the rule entity"
		+ "that settles each topic"
		IMPL "README.md::This README deliberately does not restate the"
	SPEC "The global save file schema is kept as the formal description of the format, although no"
		+ "code consumes it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json"
	REJECTED "Keeping a markdown document of the rules beside the corpus: a second copy maintained"
		+ "by hand"
	RATIONALE "The duplication had let the README claim behaviours the code did not have"
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 42

DECISION WorldObjectNamesAreAttestedBySourceOrSave
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A world object name is kept only when it is attested by the label file used as the"
		+ "inventory of group identifiers, or read in one of the reference saves"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts::labels-engplus.txt"
	SPEC "The label table and the name list constrain each other: a label without a name and a name"
		+ "without a label both fail the label spec"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.spec.ts::should find a label"
			+ "for each of them"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.spec.ts::should label no"
			+ "name the game is not known to use"
	REJECTED "Identifying a group identifier by resemblance to a wiki page title: it gave three"
		+ "machines the value of another"
	REJECTED "Replacing the repository labels with those of the attestation source: its labels are"
		+ "community-made, only its keys are the game's"
	SOURCE "Review"
		PR 43

DECISION AnErrorsOriginDecidesItsPath
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "An error on an input file the tool does not modify belongs to validation, which runs"
		+ "first; the same error arising later is a broken invariant and fails loudly"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors"
	SPEC "An error the tool creates through its own intervention (merge, renumbering,"
		+ "serialization, writing) reaches the UI and the CLI through a presenter outcome of its"
		+ "own family, never through an exception"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::this.presenter.presentMergedSaveUnusable()"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/MergeResultPresenterPort.ts::presentMergedSaveUnusable"
	SPEC "The catch is typed on the domain error, never on unknown"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts"
	REJECTED "A generic presenter outcome carrying any error"
	REJECTED "Converting every caught error into an outcome, whatever its family"
	RATIONALE "Reusing the input files outcome would tell the user their saves are bad when the"
		+ "tool is what failed"
	SOURCE "Review"
		PR 47

DECISION ABrokenInvariantFailsWithANamedErrorType
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A broken invariant of the core-mapping infrastructure fails with a named error type of"
		+ "infrastructure/errors, never with a bare Error"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors/UnexpectedSaveSectionError.ts::extends"
			+ "Error"
	SPEC "A domain rule reached with data validation should have refused fails with a named error"
		+ "type of domain/errors, never with a bare TypeError nor a bare Error; nothing catches it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/errors/NoGlobalMetadataToMergeError.ts::extends"
			+ "Error"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeGlobalMetadata.spec.ts::toThrow(NoGlobalMetadataToMergeError)"
	SPEC "The JSDoc of the error carries the instruction: fix what let the data through, never"
		+ "soften the guard"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors/UnexpectedSaveSectionError.ts::never"
			+ "soften the guard"
	REJECTED "Throwing a bare Error and telling the cases apart by their message"
	REJECTED "A silent fallback on the shape of the section: it left a whole section unvalidated"
	REJECTED "Declaring a domain error in infrastructure/errors: the domain never depends on"
		+ "infrastructure (ARCH-CA-INF-6)"
	RATIONALE "Each invariant is told apart from a programming bug by its type; the other packages"
		+ "keep a bare Error until they have a second case"
	SOURCE "Review"
		PR 48
	SOURCE "Domain layer"
		PR 102

DECISION ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "The validation result carries the warnings, never the parser"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveValidationResult.ts::warnings:"
			+ "SaveWarningCode[]"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsParserPort.ts::the single"
			+ "source of warnings"
	SPEC "Validation runs first in the four flows, and warnings are reported on every outcome,"
		+ "invalid saves and successful merges included"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application"
	REJECTED "Having the parsing port carry the warnings: two lists to reconcile in every consumer"
	SOURCE "Migration"
		PR 61

DECISION UserTextLivesInCoreMappingPresentation
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "An internal code (warning, merge failure) is turned into a sentence by the core-mapping"
		+ "presentation, in a single messages directory; the ViewModel exposes strings ready to"
		+ "display"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatSaveWarning.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages"
	SPEC "An outcome that already carries its messages gets no additional sentence"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/mergeFailureMessages.js::mergedSaveUnusableMessage"
	SPEC "An unknown code falls back to a generic message, and the code itself is never displayed"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatSaveWarning.ts::unknownSaveWarningMessage"
	REJECTED "Translating the codes in the UI: the table would be duplicated for the CLI"
	REJECTED "Displaying the internal code when no sentence exists"
	SOURCE "Migration"
		PR 61

DECISION ALocationIsABusinessLabelFollowedByTheIndex
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A validation message travels as a message and a location, null when the error concerns"
		+ "the whole file"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatValidationIssue.ts"
	SPEC "The location is a business label followed by the index, formatted in presentation; the"
		+ "ViewModel never exposes the raw indexes"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.ts"
	SPEC "The section label table is complete, and an exhaustiveness test fails as soon as a"
		+ "section is missing from it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/saveSectionLabels.js::export const"
			+ "saveSectionLabels"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.spec.ts::When the"
			+ "section has no label"
	REJECTED "The index alone: a detail of the file format"
	REJECTED "The label alone: too poor to edit the save by hand"
	REJECTED "Raw indexes in the ViewModel: each delivery mechanism would import the formatter,"
		+ "which the exports rule forbids"
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 37

DECISION BothMessageListsShareOneRendering
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A single component renders both lists; errors and warnings are told apart by the"
		+ "separation of the two lists, never by a parameter"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/validation/ValidationMessagesList.tsx"
	SPEC "A validation message reads as a stack frame: monospace, the message first, its origin"
		+ "below, prefixed and indented"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/validationMessages.js::validationMessageLocationPrefix"
	REJECTED "Parameterizing the list component by severity"
	REJECTED "Placing the location before the message: refused on a screenshot, two typefaces on"
		+ "one line"
	SOURCE "Review"
		PR 37

DECISION UiSaveManagerHasOneUiErrorIdiom
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A controller call that does not complete sets a local error signal, logs the technical"
		+ "detail, and displays a fixed sentence of the package messages"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx::console.error(error)"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/useLoadSaveFile.ts::console.error(error)"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/mergeSectionMessages.js::mergeSectionCallFailedMessage"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/displayRouteMessages.js::displayRouteCallFailedMessage"
	SPEC "The failure notice is displayed under the button that produced it, never in the area of"
		+ "the parse result"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx"
	REJECTED "Placing the failure notice where the validation messages go: off screen on a short"
		+ "window, and read as a parse result"
	REJECTED "A bare catch that logs nothing"
	SOURCE "Review"
		PR 58

DECISION ADomainRuleIgnoresValidationVocabulary
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "No file of the domain imports application"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain"
	SPEC "A domain rule returns a failure type it declares itself, without code or sentence, and"
		+ "the infrastructure translates it into a validation issue"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/validateUniqueHost.ts::UniqueHostViolation |"
			+ "null"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSaveContent.js::function"
			+ "toUniqueHostIssue"
	REJECTED "A generic domain violation type carrying a rule discriminant: it brings the code"
		+ "vocabulary back into the domain"
	REJECTED "Moving ValidationIssue and its codes into the domain: technical error codes have no"
		+ "business meaning"
	REJECTED "Throwing from the rule: validation would stop being exhaustive"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling"
		PR 62

DECISION OneModuleAloneParsesASaveLine
	SPEC "The parser is the only point of production code where a save line reaches JSON.parse;"
		+ "validation and merge both use it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	SPEC "Failure is per line and located, without taking down the valid entries around it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	REJECTED "A second parser in the validator: the divergence let validation accept a save whose"
		+ "merge lost a section"
	REJECTED "A non-lazy variant of the parser"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 47

DECISION AnInt64IdentifierIsCarriedByItsDecimalText
	SPEC "An identifier of the save format beyond the exact integer range of a double is carried by"
		+ "its exact decimal text, never by a number; any future int64 field follows it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/int64Identifiers.js::RAW_INTEGER_FIELDS"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::When a save holding an"
			+ "int64 player identifier is read back"
	SPEC "Exactness is produced and consumed in shared-save-processing alone, and the section"
		+ "schema declares a decimal string"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js::keepInt64IdentifierText"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section2-players.schema.json::Player Steam ID"
			+ "(primary key, int64)"
	REJECTED "Typing the field as BigInt: JSON.stringify throws on it and ajv cannot validate it"
	REJECTED "Keeping the raw text of the section entries: the merge rebuilds every player entry"
	REJECTED "A validation rule on integer precision: a large literal in a save is normal"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ThePlayerIdentifierIsTheOnlyInt64FieldBeyondDoubleRange
	RESTS_ON @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 49

DECISION TheFloatSuffixIsAppliedAtEmission
	SPEC "The .0 suffix of float fields is applied at emission, field by field, never by textual"
		+ "post-processing of the produced string"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.js::export function stringifyEntry"
	SPEC "A non-flat entry throws instead of being serialized silently"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.js::save entries are expected to be"
			+ "flat"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.spec.js::When a field holds a"
			+ "nested value"
	REJECTED "Textual post-processing: a sign whose player text was FLOAT:5 came out as a number"
	REJECTED "Narrowing the parameter type instead of the runtime check: the type binds only"
		+ "type-checked callers"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 36

DECISION ASchemaRuleHoldsByMeaningBeforeMeasurement
	SPEC "Every bound or schema rule holds by meaning before holding by measurement; no implication"
		+ "holding by a coincidence of the sample is written"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::\"dependencies\""
	SPEC "additionalProperties stays closed: the format is described exhaustively"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::\"additionalProperties\":"
			+ "false"
	SPEC "The ten section schemas stay in draft-07 and express their implications with dependencies"
		+ "in array form"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas"
	REJECTED "Fitting a bound to the reference saves: it refuses a legitimate save tomorrow"
	REJECTED "Deducing a missing value from a regularity observed between tiers"
	REJECTED "dependentRequired: a draft 2019-09 keyword Ajv 8 refuses under the draft-07"
		+ "meta-schema"
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 48

DECISION FloatSerializationIsCheckedInInfrastructure
	SPEC "No domain rule reads the text of a save; the float suffix check lives in infrastructure"
		+ "beside schema validation"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateFloatSerialization.ts"
	REJECTED "Checking parsed entries in the domain: after JSON.parse, 5.0 and 5 are the same"
		+ "double"
	REJECTED "Moving the check to shared-save-processing, which does not know ValidationIssue"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling"
		PR 62

DECISION AMergeTakesExactlyTwoSavesPerFolder
	SPEC "An input subfolder is merged only when it holds exactly two save files; any other count"
		+ "sets it aside, named on the error output with its count"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::MERGEABLE_SAVE_FILES_COUNT"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::renderSkippedFolder(folder,"
			+ "saveFileNames.length)"
	REJECTED "Accumulating the saves of a folder holding more than two: the UI takes two, and both"
		+ "entry points must agree"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling in review"
		PR 42

DECISION APlayerIdentityIsCarriedByItsEntry
	SPEC "The host role is applied by the position of the entry in save A, never by identifier nor"
		+ "by name; save B supplies it only when save A holds no player"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.ts::hostPositionInSaveA ==="
			+ "NO_HOST_POSITION"
	SPEC "A player identifier is never regenerated"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/resolveIdConflicts.ts::Players are left"
			+ "out"
	REJECTED "Designating the host by identifier equality: identifiers are not unique across two"
		+ "saves"
	REJECTED "Designating the host by name equality: two namesakes would both come out as hosts"
	REJECTED "A new identifier for a save B player already in save A: it would designate no real"
		+ "account"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RESTS_ON @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
	ASSUMES @HYPOTHESIS.APlayerIdentifierIsASteamAccountReusedAcrossGames
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 39
		PR 41

DECISION AMergeThatWritesAFileIsASuccess
	SPEC "The use case validates its two inputs, merges, then validates what it produced, without a"
		+ "branch"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::const mergedSaveValidation ="
			+ "this.validator.validate(fileName, content);"
	SPEC "The errors of the merged file travel in a channel of their own; a merge success carries"
		+ "the warnings of its two inputs only"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeSucceededResponse.ts::mergeErrors"
	SPEC "In the CLI, an invalid merged save does not make the exit code non-zero; a merge that"
		+ "produced nothing does"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::exitProcess(UNEXPECTED_ERROR_EXIT_CODE)"
	REJECTED "Refusing to write a file the revalidation finds invalid: the merge would depend on"
		+ "the severity of the validator"
	REJECTED "An option that skips the revalidation"
	REJECTED "Reporting the warnings of the revalidation: their vocabulary does not apply to an"
		+ "output"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 59

DECISION NoMergeWarningChannelWithoutAProducer
	SPEC "The merge exposes no warning channel on its output while no merge rule produces a"
		+ "warning; the day one does, it is a single list under one name end to end"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeSucceededResponse.ts"
	REJECTED "Opening the channel ahead of need: an empty section and an identifier collision are"
		+ "not producers"
	REJECTED "Folding the output warnings into the per-input lists"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "Pull request"
		PR 54

DECISION AMergeProducesAnOrdinarySave
	SPEC "One parser and one serializer read and write a SaveSections, when loading as when"
		+ "merging, and know nothing of a merge"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsParserPort.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsSerializerPort.ts"
	SPEC "resolveIdConflicts returns a SaveSections, entries of save A before those of save B"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/resolveIdConflicts.ts"
	SPEC "The save model of the domain lives in domain/save; merge rules receive and return it, and"
		+ "none imports a section index or the parsed tuple"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/save"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge"
	SPEC "An identifier list is read and written in shared-save-processing, beside its DTO, and"
		+ "called from the infrastructure mappers only"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/idList.js::parseIdList"
	REJECTED "A serializer specific to the merge result: a service for one case, and a merge rule"
		+ "in infrastructure"
	REJECTED "A second read port for the merge: two ports reading a save from its content"
	REJECTED "A port to name the merged file: a pure function is not an external capability"
		+ "(ARCH-CA-APP-3)"
	REJECTED "Merge rules taking wire DTO strings: the domain would parse a persistence encoding"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	SOURCE "Owner ruling in review"
		PR 62

DECISION AnEmptyMetadataSectionIsRefusedByValidation
	SPEC "Validation refuses a save whose section 0 carries no entry, before any merge"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSaveContent.js::saveFileSchema.items[GLOBAL_METADATA_SECTION_INDEX].minItems"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSaveContent.spec.js::When the"
			+ "section carries no entry"
	REJECTED "Falling back to default metadata: the merge would produce a save from two invalid"
		+ "inputs"
