DECISION ProductionIsPublishedByHandFromAReleaseTag
	SPEC "Netlify publishes no production deploy by itself; production is the deploy of the commit"
		+ "a ui-save-manager-v* tag names, published by hand"
		IMPL "README.md::Netlify publishes no production deploy by itself"
	SPEC "Deploy previews of pull requests against master stay"
		IMPL "README.md::the deploy previews stay public"
	REJECTED "Publishing every push to master: nothing chooses what reaches production"
	REJECTED "A release branch a workflow moves to each tag and Netlify builds: a second production"
		+ "branch to keep, for a publication the owner wants to make by hand"
	REJECTED "netlify deploy --prod from GitHub Actions: an access token in the repository, and the"
		+ "server function nitro builds for Netlify is not proven to deploy that way"
	RATIONALE "Netlify cannot build a git tag, and the owner wants to control what reaches"
		+ "production; the squash commit of a release pull request is both the tagged commit and a"
		+ "deploy Netlify built from master"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE83
	SOURCE "Ruled with the user on 2026-09-23 during CHORE83"
		PR 135

DECISION BothCliEntryFilesRunThroughOneSharedFunction
	SPEC "Running the command of a CLI when its module is the entry point, and exiting with its"
